-- l4 lint fixture: "subject to" and "despite" with no provision behind them are
-- English, not overrides. Nothing is reported, not even as set aside.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is subject to tax in the territory it comes from` n MEANS
        "unless the person is subject to the process of the court,"
    ... n GREATER THAN 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my employer cannot find me a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts` n MEANS
    n GREATER THAN 2
